Short:        Rescue the council in a platform game
Author:       Omnispeak authors; Amiga port by Christopher Reemts
Uploader:     mail@rootroot.de (Christopher Reemts)
Type:         game/jump
Version:      0.1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Requires:     68040/FPU, RTG, AHI, Keen 4 v1.4 EGA data

Keen 4 for AmigaOS 68k, based on Omnispeak.
Needs an accelerator, 68040/FPU and 256-color RTG output.
Tested on PiStorm/Emu68. Other accelerators are untested.
No OCS or AGA output. Further work depends on interest and feedback.

Game data is not included. Get the v1.4 EGA shareware archive here:
https://davidgow.net/keen/4keen14.zip
GT retail data is not compatible.

Installation
------------
Extract the LHA archive into a writable drawer.

Installer: requires Installer 43.3+, UnZip, IconX and about 700 KiB
free in T:. Start Install, choose Intermediate User, select the parent
drawer for Keen4, then select 4keen14.zip. Existing saves and settings
are preserved. Installer 44.10 stalled in Expert mode.
Installer: util/misc/Installer-43_3 on Aminet.

Manual: extract AUDIO.CK4, EGAGRAPH.CK4 and GAMEMAPS.CK4 from the ZIP
beside omnispeak. Keep the other files from the LHA archive together.
Start with Execute Start-Keen4 in a Shell, or double-click Start-Keen4
if IconX is installed. Start-Keen4-NoSound disables audio.

Controls and sound
------------------
Arrow keys move, Ctrl jumps, Alt uses the pogo stick, Space fires.
Enter shows status. F5 quick-saves, F9 quick-loads.
Controls can be changed under Main Menu > Configure.

For a two-button joystick, enable Two-Button Firing in Configure >
Options. Button 0 jumps, button 1 uses the pogo; both buttons fire.

Sound uses AHI Unit 0. The default stream is 22050 Hz, 16-bit mono.
Sample rate, channel count and buffer size can be set in OMNISPK.CFG.
See the included README for details.

Testing
-------
Gameplay, sound, joystick input and save/load work on an A1200 with
PiStorm32-Lite and CM4. A full playthrough and long sessions have not
been verified.

Credits and source
------------------
Based on Omnispeak: https://github.com/sulix/omnispeak
Authors and license terms are in AUTHORS and LICENSE. Engine and SDL
source are included in the source drawer; third-party notices are in
licenses and the source tree. Game data must be supplied separately.

Project: https://github.com/rootrootde/keen4-amiga

Changes in 0.1.0
---------------
First Amiga RTG release, with AHI sound, keyboard and joystick input,
and an Amiga Installer script.
